  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The `JWSRenewalInfo` type is a string of three Base64 URL-encoded components, separated by a period. The string contains the JWS representation of the subscription renewal information, signed by the App Store according to the JSON Web Signature (JWS) `https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7515` specification.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreservernotifications/documentation/AppStoreServerNotifications/JWSRenewalInfo",
            "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7515"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The three components in the string are a header, a payload, and a signature, in that order.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "To read the subscription renewal information, Base64 URL-decode the payload. Use a `JWSRenewalInfoDecodedPayload` object to read the payload information.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreservernotifications/documentation/AppStoreServerNotifications/JWSRenewalInfoDecodedPayload"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To read the header, Base64 URL-decode it and use a `JWSDecodedHeader` object to access the information. Use the information in the header to verify the signature.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreservernotifications/documentation/AppStoreServerNotifications/JWSDecodedHeader"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
